WEBVTT

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.882
♪ ♪

00:00:11.052 --> 00:00:12.804
( sheep bleating )

00:00:17.433 --> 00:00:18.976
Oh!

00:00:23.481 --> 00:00:25.900
I’d rather not
talk about this one.

00:00:27.568 --> 00:00:30.196
( bleating )

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.247
This is the puppet hospital
and burn center.

00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:46.587
It’s relatively new.

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:54.971
Ah, the administration offices.

00:00:56.305 --> 00:00:57.974
Hello, Doris.

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:05.439
( machines whir )

00:01:12.613 --> 00:01:14.532
( rapid gunfire )

00:01:19.704 --> 00:01:22.248
( gunfire )

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:29.213
( gun powers up )

00:01:30.631 --> 00:01:33.217
( popping, fizzing )

00:01:33.301 --> 00:01:35.428
Why is everything here
completely pointless?

00:01:35.469 --> 00:01:38.180
Candy doesn’t have
to have a point.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.473
That’s why it’s candy.

00:01:39.557 --> 00:01:41.517
MIKE:
It’s stupid!

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:45.605
DR. WONKA ( voice-over ):
Candy is a waste of time.

00:01:45.646 --> 00:01:49.191
No son of mine is going to be
a chocolatier.

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.486
Then I’ll run away...
to Switzerland,

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:53.696
Bavaria,

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:55.990
the candy capitals
of the world.

00:01:56.032 --> 00:01:57.450
Go ahead.

00:01:57.491 --> 00:02:00.161
But I won’t be here
when you come back.

00:02:06.709 --> 00:02:08.961
( gloves squeak )

00:02:17.303 --> 00:02:20.681
( grand adventurous theme
playing )

00:02:28.522 --> 00:02:29.857
Sorry, son.

00:02:29.899 --> 00:02:32.193
We’re closing
for the night.

00:02:41.994 --> 00:02:44.705
( light, mysterious theme plays
)

00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:50.544
( thunder crashing )

00:02:51.712 --> 00:02:55.091
( explosions )

00:02:57.885 --> 00:02:58.970
I want to pick a room.

00:02:59.053 --> 00:03:02.014
( gunfire, explosions )

00:03:02.056 --> 00:03:03.557
Go ahead.

00:03:07.061 --> 00:03:08.270
( dings )

00:03:16.904 --> 00:03:18.739
( dings )

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.743
( electronic blipping )

00:03:22.785 --> 00:03:24.328
Here.

00:03:24.412 --> 00:03:27.623
Put these on quick and don’t
take them off whatever you do.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:29.291
This light could

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:31.252
burn your eyeballs
right out of your skulls.

00:03:31.335 --> 00:03:34.088
And we certainly don’t
want that, now, do we?

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:38.926
This is the testing room

00:03:39.010 --> 00:03:41.012
for my very latest
and greatest invention--

00:03:41.095 --> 00:03:43.806
television chocolate.

00:03:43.889 --> 00:03:45.099
One day, it occurred to me:

00:03:45.141 --> 00:03:48.227
Hey, if television
can break up a photograph

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:50.396
into millions and millions
of tiny little pieces

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:52.189
and send it
whizzing through the air

00:03:52.273 --> 00:03:54.108
then reassemble it
on the other end--

00:03:54.191 --> 00:03:56.485
why can’t I do the
same thing with chocolate?

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:59.155
Why can’t I send
a real bar of chocolate

00:03:59.238 --> 00:04:02.450
through the television,
all ready to be eaten?

00:04:02.491 --> 00:04:05.161
I’m not gonna touch it.
I’m not going in that direction.

00:04:05.244 --> 00:04:06.620
( applause )

00:04:06.662 --> 00:04:07.955
( remote clicks )
( "Macarena" plays )

00:04:08.039 --> 00:04:09.040
( remote clicks )
Sounds impossible.

00:04:09.123 --> 00:04:10.708
MIKE:
It is impossible.

00:04:10.791 --> 00:04:13.961
You don’t understand
anything about science.

00:04:14.003 --> 00:04:16.839
First off,
there’s a difference between

00:04:16.922 --> 00:04:18.340
waves and particles.

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:20.009
Duh!

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:21.802
Second, the amount of
power it would take

00:04:21.886 --> 00:04:23.471
to convert energy
into matter

00:04:23.512 --> 00:04:25.639
would be like nine atomic bombs.

00:04:25.723 --> 00:04:27.391
Mumbler!

00:04:27.475 --> 00:04:28.642
Seriously...

00:04:28.726 --> 00:04:32.229
I cannot understand
a single word you’re saying.

00:04:35.524 --> 00:04:36.859
Okeydokey.

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.986
I shall now send a bar
of chocolate

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.362
from one end of the room

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:43.741
to the other by television.

00:04:43.824 --> 00:04:45.493
Bring in the chocolate!

00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:53.667
( "Also Sprach Zarathustra"
playing )

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:05.304
( music building
dramatically )

00:05:05.346 --> 00:05:07.348
It’s got to be real big.

00:05:07.389 --> 00:05:10.184
’Cause you know how on TV
you can film a regular-size man

00:05:10.226 --> 00:05:11.852
and he comes out
looking this tall?

00:05:11.936 --> 00:05:13.562
Same basic principle.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:17.233
( dramatic music continues )

00:05:21.904 --> 00:05:24.240
( dramatic theme continues )

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:36.335
( dramatic theme continues )

00:05:45.719 --> 00:05:46.971
It’s gone.

00:05:47.054 --> 00:05:49.807
Told you.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:51.016
That bar of chocolate is now

00:05:51.058 --> 00:05:52.560
rushing through the air
above our heads

00:05:52.601 --> 00:05:55.020
in a million tiny little pieces.

00:05:55.062 --> 00:05:56.063
Come over here.

00:05:56.105 --> 00:05:58.482
Come on, come on.
Come on.

00:06:03.404 --> 00:06:06.365
Watch the screen.

00:06:08.826 --> 00:06:10.744
Here it comes.

00:06:10.786 --> 00:06:12.830
Look.

00:06:16.917 --> 00:06:18.002
Take it.

00:06:18.085 --> 00:06:20.087
It’s just a picture on a screen.

00:06:20.171 --> 00:06:21.922
Scaredy cat.

00:06:22.006 --> 00:06:23.549
You take it.

00:06:24.592 --> 00:06:27.261
Go on.
Just reach out and grab it.

00:06:34.768 --> 00:06:36.270
Go on.

